      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/43a26b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-20T03:32:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Since Daniel Lew's Sentinels randomizer is only available for androad, I've decided to make a randomizer for iOS. &nbsp;You can get it here:&nbsp;<span>(</span><a href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/sentinels-multiverse-randomizer/id791098197?mt=8&amp;ign-mpt=uo%3D4\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/sentinels-multiverse-randomizer/id791098197?mt=8&amp;ign-mpt=uo%3D4</a><span>)</span></p><p><font size=\"2\">The Randomizer uses a point based system to estimate difficulty levels. The system is similar to the SotM score system (</font><a href=\"http://x.gray.org/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-difficulty-scores.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://x.gray.org/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-difficulty-scores.htm</a>l<font size=\"2\">), but uses a slightly different statistical model.</font></p><p>If you have any questions, comments, or suggestions, let me know.</p><p>Screenshot: http://imgur.com/WcTKndO</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:02.855Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
